WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.210
Destiny. Fate. Dreams.

3
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.830
These unstoppable ideals are
held deep in the heart of man.

4
00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:25.340
As long as there are people
who seek freedom in this life,

5
00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.010
these things shall not
vanish from the earth!

6
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.800
<b>Landfall in Alabasta</b>

7
00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:58.470
<b>Nanohana
Kingdom of Alabasta</b>

8
00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.950
So this is an Alabasta city.

9
00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.610
Is there food?

10
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.070
Listen carefully, guys.

11
00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.490
I want you all to do your best
to control yourselves

12
00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:19.540
while we're here.

13
00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.660
Of course, Nami.

14
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.990
You do realize the one who needs
to hear that warning

15
00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:25.500
the most has already
abandoned ship.

16
00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:29.210
Feed me now!

17
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:29.210
Get back here!

18
00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:31.380
He doesn't know
the meaning of control.

19
00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.380
What now?

20
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.090
He's easy to find.

21
00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:36.060
Just look for the area
with the commotion,

22
00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.850
and that's where he'll be.

23
00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.470
He's right.

24
00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:41.470
Ugh. I wish he'd at least remember

25
00:02:41.470 --> 00:02:43.810
that he has a bounty
on that rubbery head of his.

26
00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:46.230
Especially while we're
in a big country like this.

27
00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:48.400
Forget about Luffy.
He can take care of himself.

28
00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.480
Now let's go find some food.
We can get to work after that.

29
00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:53.740
They're all the same!

30
00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:57.950
What's wrong, Karoo?

31
00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.620
Mr. 3's ship!

32
00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.500
I thought we took care of
that creep for good already.

33
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.710
I'm certain it's him.

34
00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:07.710
That ship couldn't
even run without Mr. 3's

35
00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.250
Wax-Wax Fruit powers.

36
00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:10.750
The bastard's here.

37
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:12.130
This isn't good.

38
00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:21.260
Give me food!

39
00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.310
What's with this
weirdo city, anyway?

40
00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:26.230
There's some strange non-food smell
all over the place!

41
00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:29.480
There's one! It's a restaurant!

42
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.740
So... what do you want
from me now, Captain?

43
00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.700
I'd just like you to come
with me quietly.

44
00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:42.660
No, thanks. I think I'll pass.

45
00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.870
Yeah... figured you'd say that.

46
00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:51.920
I'm here in Alabasta trying
to hunt down another pirate at the moment.

47
00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:55.720
To be honest, I have no real interest
in capturing you right now.

48
00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.590
Then just look the other way.

49
00:03:57.590 --> 00:03:59.720
I'm afraid I can't do that.

50
00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:01.600
Not as long as I'm a Marine,

51
00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:05.390
and you're part
of a notorious pirate crew.

52
00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.890
That's not much
of a reason, now is it?

53
00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:10.770
How 'bout I give you one?

54
00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:18.240
Give me food!

55
00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.450
Gum-Gum Rocket!

56
00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.300
Woo, food! Now I can eat!

57
00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.510
Finally! I'm starving!
I thought I was gonna die!

58
00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.850
Old guy, gimme food.
Hurry, come on.

59
00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.140
Food, food, food, food!
Now, now, now!

60
00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.310
Wow!

61
00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.810
This is beautiful!

62
00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:56.280
<b>On the Outskirts
of Nanohana</b>

63
00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:55.980
Oh, yeah! Love it!

64
00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.740
Uh... well, I know I asked you
to pick out some clothes for us,

65
00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:02.530
but these were meant
for dancer girls.

66
00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.160
Oh, Vivi! You're a vision.

67
00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.200
But commoners wouldn't wear this.

68
00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.790
But aren't dancers common?

69
00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.870
We're crossing a desert!

70
00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:10.870
Hey, don't worry!

71
00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.670
If you get tired, my darling,
I'll just carry you!

72
00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:16.170
This is pointless.

73
00:05:16.670 --> 00:05:18.920
Now then, let's take
a look at you guys.

74
00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:22.010
Compared to the lovely ladies,
you two look like sloppy bandits.

75
00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:23.720
You might wanna look in a mirror.

76
00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:24.640
Hey, Chopper!

77
00:05:24.640 --> 00:05:26.260
What are you doing?

78
00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.180
It's that smell!

79
00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.810
Oh, yeah, where did you run off to?

80
00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:30.730
Just somewhere.

81
00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:32.100
Is he not feeling well?

82
00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.110
Yeah, it's just the perfume.
Chopper can't stand it.

83
00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:36.360
Perfume?

84
00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:39.780
Oh, yeah, Tony has
an incredibly sensitive nose.

85
00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.070
This stuff?

86
00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.910
Some of it does have
a really strong smell.

87
00:05:42.910 --> 00:05:44.070
Oh...

88
00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.790
Ahh! Stop!

89
00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.790
You smell just like an angel
in a field of fresh flowers!

90
00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.790
You're an idiot.

91
00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:49.790
Huh?!

92
00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:53.420
At any rate, at least we've
managed to gather all the supplies

93
00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.710
that we're gonna need
to cross the desert.

94
00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:55.750
Yeah...

95
00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:58.960
This oasis... You said
it's called Yuba, right?

96
00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:03.380
Yes, that's correct. But first we'll
have to travel through the desert.

97
00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:07.810
Amazing! This is seriously
the best food I've ever tasted!

98
00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:12.230
Uh, yes... thanks a lot.
But, you see, sir...

99
00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:17.690
It's just, well...
you might want to start running now.

100
00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:18.570
Why is that?

101
00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:22.570
Damn it.

102
00:06:23.150 --> 00:06:25.110
So what the hell was that?

103
00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.120
What just happened?

104
00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:33.040
This is ridiculous!
Just look at this place!

105
00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:40.250
Oh, hi there. Many apologies
for disturbing your meal.

106
00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:49.680
What kind of world-class idiot
would do something like this?

107
00:06:58.210 --> 00:06:59.020
Hey, Luf–

108
00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.650
Straw Hat!

109
00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:13.160
I've been looking for you, Straw Hat.

110
00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.540
I thought you'd be here.
Seems I was correct.

111
00:07:22.130 --> 00:07:23.340
Would you quit eating?!

112
00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:31.260
Isn't he...?

113
00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:35.770
I'm Captain Smoker of the Marines,

114
00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:37.980
and I'm in charge of keeping
the peace in this town.

115
00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.780
You're that smoky guy!
What're you doing in Alabasta?!

116
00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.070
Wait a sec!

117
00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:52.080
Thanks a lot for the meal.

118
00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.040
Stop, you!

119
00:07:58.120 --> 00:08:00.170
Wait up, Luffy! It's me!

120
00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:04.670
Hold on a second! Hey!
Come back, Luffy!

121
00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.130
They didn't pay.

122
00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:12.260
This is bad! My Gum-Gum moves
don't work against this guy at all!

123
00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.140
I just have to make a run for it now!

124
00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:15.180
Tashigi!

125
00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:18.690
Yes, sir! Would you like
a cool towel? It's quite refreshing.

126
00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:20.150
This desert kingdom really is hot.

127
00:08:20.150 --> 00:08:22.440
Catch that guy! It's Straw Hat!

128
00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.230
Yes, sir!

129
00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:25.150
I've got him!

130
00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.830
Tashigi! Gather the Marines at once!

131
00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.660
Search every inch of this place
for the rest of his crew!

132
00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.370
Right! Come on!

133
00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.040
They must have devil fruit powers.

134
00:08:40.370 --> 00:08:41.040
No way!

135
00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.300
The Straw Hat's crew is here.
That must mean...

136
00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:51.220
Roronoa Zoro is
in the city somewhere!

137
00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:56.060
White Snake!

138
00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:03.230
Where could Luffy have gone?
He doesn't know the island at all.

139
00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:06.320
Seriously. A crew shouldn't
have to work this hard to keep track

140
00:09:06.320 --> 00:09:07.610
of their captain.

141
00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:08.400
Oh, Nami!

142
00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:09.900
This doesn't look good.

143
00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:13.410
We could be in some serious trouble
if we don't get out of here soon.

144
00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.620
Trouble? Why's that?

145
00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.120
'Cause the Marines are here.

146
00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:17.120
Marines?

147
00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.160
Let's just find Luffy
as fast as possible

148
00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.870
and get out of this town
as soon as we can.

149
00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:21.580
Hey, hide!

150
00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:22.750
What for?

151
00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.750
Wh-What was that?

152
00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:27.750
It's the Marines.

153
00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:29.670
Yeah, and they're
excited about something.

154
00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:32.630
Don't let that pirate
escape! After him!

155
00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.970
I'm sure it's nothing.
They're probably chasing some idiot pirate

156
00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.310
who's running crazy around town.

157
00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:42.850
– It's Luffy!
– It's Luffy!

158
00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.690
Oh, hey, Zoro! What's up?

159
00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:49.860
Oh, so that's where
you guys have been!

160
00:09:49.860 --> 00:09:52.030
No, you moron!
Get rid of them first!

161
00:09:55.030 --> 00:09:57.330
Well... they're coming!
What should we do now?

162
00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.740
We've got to get going!

163
00:09:58.740 --> 00:09:59.490
To the ship!

164
00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.290
Don't just stand there! We gotta go!

165
00:10:01.290 --> 00:10:02.410
– Wait up!
– Wait up!

166
00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.170
Stop right there, pirates!

167
00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.170
You can fall back now, men.

168
00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:06.880
Captain!

169
00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:09.460
That Straw Hat is mine to finish!

170
00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.610
Not good! Here he comes!

171
00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:12.800
White Blow!

172
00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:14.050
Not good!

173
00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.390
Not good! Not good! Not good!
Not good! Not good! Not good!

174
00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:19.720
Heat Haze!

175
00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:31.740
You again...

176
00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:34.200
Just give it up.

177
00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:40.830
While you may have
the power of smoke, mine is fire.

178
00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:43.290
A fight between the two of us
would be pointless.

179
00:10:43.290 --> 00:10:44.710
It would probably go on forever.

180
00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.960
All right, looks like the mystery man
 has devil fruit powers.

181
00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:49.460
Who is this guy anyway?

182
00:10:49.960 --> 00:10:50.920
That you, Ace?

183
00:10:51.800 --> 00:10:53.920
You haven't changed a bit, Luffy.

184
00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:56.090
It is you! Really?

185
00:10:56.090 --> 00:10:58.390
Wow, did you eat
a devil fruit or something?

186
00:10:58.390 --> 00:11:00.390
Yeah! The Flame-Flame Fruit.

187
00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:02.850
We'll secure the perimeter,
Captain Smoker.

188
00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:05.140
Anyway, now's probably
not the time for chatting.

189
00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:07.060
You guys get out of here.
I'll catch up.

190
00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:08.860
Don't worry about
these guys. I've got 'em.

191
00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:09.810
Go on!

192
00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:10.730
Let's go!

193
00:11:10.730 --> 00:11:11.780
Yeah! Coming!

194
00:11:12.610 --> 00:11:13.610
But, Luffy!

195
00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:15.780
Who is that guy back there?

196
00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:20.120
Whoa, how did he do that?

197
00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:34.510
White...

198
00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:35.800
Spark!

199
00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:45.140
A fire!

200
00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.480
That's no ordinary fire!

201
00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:50.310
What's going on back there?

202
00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:52.900
Looks like a fight
between smoke and fire!

203
00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:56.360
So that's the kind of power you get
after eating a Flame-Flame Fruit.

204
00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:00.490
Speaking of devil fruit,
Luffy, is it true?

205
00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.330
Is that guy really your brother?

206
00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:04.200
Yep! His name's Ace!

207
00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:07.580
Look, I'm not surprised to hear
you have a brother, Luffy.

208
00:12:07.580 --> 00:12:09.750
But what's he doing
here on the Grand Line?

209
00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:11.630
Ace is a pirate, too, just like I am!

210
00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:15.210
He left home three years before
I did to go search for the One Piece!

211
00:12:20.930 --> 00:12:23.970
Anyway, he bought us some time,
so we can't waste it!

212
00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.390
Let's get back to the ship!

213
00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:26.980
Sure, Nami dear!

214
00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.850
Wow, I never woulda thought

215
00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:36.110
I'd run into my big brother
in a place like this!

216
00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:40.990
Agh! Which way do we go?!

217
00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:43.080
Left, Usopp! Everyone, get that?!

218
00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:45.290
Yes, Nami. I'll follow
you wherever you go!

219
00:12:45.290 --> 00:12:47.200
You lovesick freak!

220
00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.710
Whoa!

221
00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:55.880
A fight between flame and smoke
is ultimately pointless.

222
00:12:57.090 --> 00:12:58.920
As we've just made obvious.

223
00:13:00.180 --> 00:13:02.430
Where's the Straw Hat
and his crew?

224
00:13:02.430 --> 00:13:03.600
They're gone, sir!

225
00:13:03.600 --> 00:13:05.890
So is Ace! We've lost sight of him!

226
00:13:06.390 --> 00:13:08.850
I run into the Straw Hat
in the Grand Line

227
00:13:08.850 --> 00:13:10.890
and have him as good as captured.

228
00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:14.980
But then, you just had to
get in my way, didn't you, Ace?

229
00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.760
Get everything stowed!
We're shoving off right away!

230
00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:19.950
Aye, aye!

231
00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:21.990
Set the sails!

232
00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:27.040
But it took us so long
to finally get here,

233
00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:29.120
and now we're leaving already, Vivi?

234
00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.330
Yes, but remember, we only stopped here
to get the supplies we're going

235
00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:33.750
to need for the rest of the journey.

236
00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.210
And now that we have all of them,

237
00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:37.750
we're going to head upriver
into the interior of Alabasta.

238
00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:41.550
Our next destination is...
the City of Green, Erumalu.

239
00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:43.180
Erumalu?

240
00:13:43.180 --> 00:13:44.180
Hurry!

241
00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:44.850
I am!

242
00:13:44.850 --> 00:13:45.850
Pick up the pace!

243
00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:46.890
Ready!

244
00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:48.430
Right! Set sail!

245
00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.690
Ah, damn it.

246
00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:57.900
You know, I have the strangest feeling
we're forgetting something.

247
00:13:58.360 --> 00:13:59.400
What the...?

248
00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:03.490
Huh, well, that's weird.

249
00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.290
Now they're all gone.
Where'd they go?

250
00:14:09.790 --> 00:14:14.170
Well, I guess giving you
a chance to escape was pointless.

251
00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:15.540
Hey!

252
00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.040
Hiya, Ace!

253
00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.710
It's been a while, hasn't it?

254
00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.510
You could say that!

255
00:14:27.550 --> 00:14:28.810
How many years has it been?

256
00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.350
Eh, I don't know.

257
00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.350
But you haven't changed
much over that time.

258
00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.770
You're a little taller,
but you pretty much look the same.

259
00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:38.520
So do you. Aside from those powers
you got from eating that devil fruit,

260
00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:40.280
you haven't changed a bit!

261
00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.490
'Member when you used to sneak
into the fields, eat a hundred

262
00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:46.280
watermelons, spit the seeds out
like a Gatling gun, and run away?!

263
00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:48.740
No, that wasn't me. That was you!

264
00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:51.910
The farmers would chase you,
and you'd scream like a girl!

265
00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:54.750
That was you too!
I watched and laughed!

266
00:15:02.210 --> 00:15:04.220
I guess we're still the same!

267
00:15:04.220 --> 00:15:05.260
Sure are!

268
00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.180
Just like old times!

269
00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:09.140
Wait...

270
00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:11.600
Wasn't your crew looking
for you a few minutes ago?

271
00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:12.220
Yeah.

272
00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.940
Hey. What are you doing
in this country, anyway?

273
00:15:15.940 --> 00:15:17.810
Huh! I take it you never received

274
00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:19.940
the message I left for you
back on Drum Island.

275
00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:21.190
Message?

276
00:15:21.690 --> 00:15:26.150
Well... I guess that's a no.
But don't worry. It's no big deal.

277
00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.820
It was just to let you know
that I'd be in Alabasta for a few days.

278
00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.200
I'm in these waters
on some business.

279
00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:33.160
Business, huh?

280
00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:37.170
Yeah, I'm with
the Whitebeard Pirates.

281
00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:38.020
Catch!

282
00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.670
The Whitebeard Pirates?

283
00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:43.300
See this tattoo? That's our mark.

284
00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:44.720
And it's my pride.

285
00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:50.680
So, Luffy! Why don't you
and your friends come join us?

286
00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:52.470
Come on, it'll be fun!
Whaddaya say?

287
00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:54.520
No, thanks.

288
00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:59.060
Ah, I had a feeling you'd say that.

289
00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:00.860
That's too bad, 'cause you see,

290
00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:03.440
Whitebeard's the greatest
pirate I've ever met.

291
00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:08.490
That's why I'm going to help him
become King of the Pirates.

292
00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:10.870
And not you, Luffy. Sorry.

293
00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:13.910
That's fine. I guess
we'll just have to fight then.

294
00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.000
Because I'm gonna be
King of the Pirates!

295
00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.300
Stop it! Don't drink it all,
you mooch! Hey!

296
00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:33.350
Something big
must be going on in town.

297
00:16:33.350 --> 00:16:35.430
All the Marines on board
wouldn't have left me

298
00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:37.770
and the ship unattended
like this if there wasn't!

299
00:16:39.690 --> 00:16:40.850
Oh, well, whatever it is,

300
00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:43.230
it's given me a perfect
opportunity to escape!

301
00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:45.730
Mr. 11.

302
00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:52.820
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

303
00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:49.360
Well now, since you know
my codename, that can only mean

304
00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:51.700
that the three of you
are members of Baroque Works!

305
00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:52.820
I'd guess millions.

306
00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:57.370
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

307
00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:54.830
Hurry up and untie me!

308
00:16:54.830 --> 00:16:57.540
You're right about one thing.
We're with Baroque Works.

309
00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:01.830
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

310
00:16:57.540 --> 00:17:00.210
But we're in line to become
number agents, you see.

311
00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:01.830
We're not millions. We're billions.

312
00:17:01.830 --> 00:17:09.800
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

313
00:17:02.170 --> 00:17:05.370
You are a numbered agent,
but looks like you're barely one at that.

314
00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:08.380
A stronger agent would have never
been captured by the Marines like this.

315
00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:09.800
Can we discuss this later?

316
00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.070
Like when I'm not tied up, maybe?

317
00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:14.760
Now help another member out
before all those Marines come back!

318
00:17:15.140 --> 00:17:17.520
Heh, heh. Oh, we'll help you, all right!

319
00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:18.060
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

320
00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:25.480
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

321
00:17:19.140 --> 00:17:23.230
Right off this mortal coil,
that is! A billions can get promoted

322
00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:25.650
to a number agent whenever
there's a seat to fill!

323
00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:25.570
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

324
00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.030
And your position
is about to be empty.

325
00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:32.490
Wait! No, hold on!

326
00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:40.010
Hey!

327
00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.880
You won't believe it!
Fire Fist Ace is here!

328
00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:46.500
What?!

329
00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:50.970
<b>Full
Fledged</b>

330
00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:47.670
Fire Fist Ace?!

331
00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:50.970
You mean the Second Division
 commander of the Whitebeard Pirates?!

332
00:17:51.760 --> 00:17:54.140
If we can take someone
with his reputation down,

333
00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:56.220
then we're guaranteed
to become number agents!

334
00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:04.810
Um, is it okay for a ship
to set sail without its captain on board?

335
00:18:05.150 --> 00:18:07.900
The first place the Marines
are gonna look for us is the harbor.

336
00:18:07.900 --> 00:18:10.030
So our top priority
is to hide the ship.

337
00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:13.030
I know of a secluded cove that's up ahead.
We can anchor the ship there.

338
00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:14.700
All right, so we lay low,

339
00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.990
let things cool down a bit,
and then go back for Luffy.

340
00:18:17.330 --> 00:18:20.950
Good grief! That guy attracts trouble
just like a dead guy attracts vultures.

341
00:18:21.500 --> 00:18:22.230
Yeah...

342
00:18:23.090 --> 00:18:25.920
That's the only reliable
thing our captain ever does.

343
00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:29.840
Here we are!

344
00:18:29.840 --> 00:18:31.800
You see your ship?

345
00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.510
Hm...

346
00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:35.430
You can't escape from us!

347
00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:36.510
Oh! There it is!

348
00:18:39.350 --> 00:18:43.180
Hey, over here,
you guys! We're here!

349
00:18:43.180 --> 00:18:46.230
Luffy, you go on ahead
and– Oh, you already went.

350
00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:48.110
Oh, I don't believe it.

351
00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:51.940
I found Luffy!

352
00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:52.820
Are you sure?

353
00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:55.570
Yeah, that stupid mug
is definitely his.

354
00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:56.280
Uh-oh.

355
00:19:00.490 --> 00:19:02.580
Hey, guys!

356
00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.740
Sanji! Tony! Are you all right?!

357
00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:09.170
Oh, Luffy came back.

358
00:19:09.170 --> 00:19:10.800
Yeah, the hard way.

359
00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:14.800
Sorry 'bout that, guys. My bad.

360
00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:17.970
Yeah, you're sorry, all right!
The sorriest excuse for a captain

361
00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:19.640
who's ever sailed
the sea, you moron!

362
00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:22.350
Do you have any idea
how much trouble you've put us in?

363
00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:25.020
Can't you at least try and act
like a captain sometime?

364
00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:29.150
I'm sorry... Oh!
That's right! Where's Ace?

365
00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:29.730
Ace?

366
00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:31.480
You were with your brother, huh?

367
00:19:31.480 --> 00:19:34.440
Wait a minute. You didn't
just leave him, did you?

368
00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:38.240
Um, sorta, but don't worry.
Ace is really strong.

369
00:19:38.240 --> 00:19:40.030
So how strong is he?

370
00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.740
Well, let me put it like this.

371
00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.500
When we were younger,
I was never able to beat him in a fight,

372
00:19:44.500 --> 00:19:47.500
and this was way back in the days
before he ate a Flame-Flame Fruit!

373
00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:49.960
That's how strong my big brother is!

374
00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:52.800
You mean there's a flesh-and-blood person
that you couldn't beat?!

375
00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:55.470
The big brother of a monster
is an even bigger monster.

376
00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:59.550
I guess so, 'cause Ace
used to beat me up all the time.

377
00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:02.390
But I bet now
I could kick his big butt!

378
00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:05.180
I'd like to see you try
and back that claim up.

379
00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:11.520
So... exactly whose butt's...
getting kicked?

380
00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:16.320
Oh, hey, Ace! This is my crew
I was telling you about!

381
00:20:16.320 --> 00:20:19.410
Nice to meet you, and thanks
for taking care of my kid brother!

382
00:20:19.410 --> 00:20:20.740
I know he's a handful!

383
00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.160
– Oh, no, not at all.
– Oh, no, not at all.

384
00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:25.540
Come on, be honest.
This is Luffy we're talking about!

385
00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:27.620
Isn't he a bit much for you
to handle at times?

386
00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.460
– Not at all.
– Not at all.

387
00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:31.380
You're good people.

388
00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:33.630
Well, sit down and relax.

389
00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:36.130
I'm sure you two
have lots of catching up to do.

390
00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:36.840
I'll make some tea.

391
00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:39.890
No, that's thoughtful,
but I don't want to impose.

392
00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:46.020
He's not exactly what I expected.

393
00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:47.230
I'll say.

394
00:20:48.390 --> 00:20:51.770
He's polite, helpful, and gracious,
the polar opposite of Luffy.

395
00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.020
One of 'em only cares
about stuffing his face.

396
00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:55.900
There's no way
these two can be brothers!

397
00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.110
While the other
only cares about his brother!

398
00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:00.530
I wish I had a wonderful
brother like that!

399
00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:03.450
Brother? I wish I had
a wonderful captain like that.

400
00:21:03.450 --> 00:21:05.410
Sanji! He's kidding!

401
00:21:05.410 --> 00:21:08.250
See! I told you
they were interesting.

402
00:21:11.960 --> 00:21:14.540
Baroque Works! Those are
the billions' ships!

403
00:21:14.540 --> 00:21:17.510
Are we going to let them escape
from the billions?!

404
00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:19.510
– No way!
– No way!

405
00:21:19.510 --> 00:21:22.260
We'll show 'em what
Baroque Works' billions are made of!

406
00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:23.180
Full speed ahead!

407
00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:24.930
Those guys again?

408
00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:26.640
– Luffy.
– Hm?

409
00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.140
Leave it to me. I'll handle them.

410
00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:32.350
He's going all by himself?

411
00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:34.190
And in that dinky boat too.

412
00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.070
I wouldn't worry about him
if I were you.

413
00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:40.740
They don't let just anyone become
the Second Division commander

414
00:21:40.740 --> 00:21:42.360
of the Whitebeard Pirates.

415
00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:45.780
Is he insane?! Fire Fist
is heading right towards us!

416
00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:49.330
Let him come! Our ships are gonna
make matchsticks out of his!

417
00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:53.210
He jumped!

418
00:21:54.130 --> 00:21:55.460
Open fire!

419
00:21:55.460 --> 00:21:57.800
Blow him to pieces, men!

420
00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:09.600
Fire Fist!

421
00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:34.210
He roasted them!

422
00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:47.220
Captain Smoker!

423
00:22:47.930 --> 00:22:49.510
We've combed the entire city, sir,

424
00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:52.310
but Straw Hat Luffy and his crew
are nowhere to be found.

425
00:22:52.310 --> 00:22:54.690
Do you wanna know
who I saw with them?

426
00:22:55.190 --> 00:22:57.690
Vivi, and I'm certain
it was her too.

427
00:22:57.690 --> 00:23:00.360
Vivi? As in Princess Vivi Nefertari?

428
00:23:00.360 --> 00:23:02.820
But what would she be doing
with the Straw Hat Pirates?

429
00:23:02.820 --> 00:23:04.280
She must be their hostage.

430
00:23:04.280 --> 00:23:05.950
They probably
abducted her in the hopes

431
00:23:05.950 --> 00:23:08.620
that her father would pay
a hefty ransom.

432
00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:11.410
Doubt it. She wasn't
acting like a kidnap victim,

433
00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:12.450
more like part of the crew.

434
00:23:12.450 --> 00:23:16.420
The princess... acting like a pirate?

435
00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:20.550
Something strange is happening.
I just wish I knew what it was.

436
00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:22.550
Captain Smoker!

437
00:23:22.550 --> 00:23:23.840
I'm sorry, sir!

438
00:23:23.840 --> 00:23:26.430
But it appears that Mr. 11
was killed on board the ship

439
00:23:26.430 --> 00:23:28.550
while we were off searching
for the Straw Hats!

440
00:23:28.550 --> 00:23:31.180
Who, by the way,
we still haven't located yet!

441
00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:33.140
Call off the search
for Straw Hat Luffy.

442
00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:35.350
I have a pretty good idea
where he's headed.

443
00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:38.020
He's after Crocodile. I'm sure of it.

444
00:23:38.020 --> 00:23:39.860
Why Crocodile?

445
00:23:39.860 --> 00:23:41.980
He's one of the Seven
Warlords of the Sea!

446
00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:44.780
A pirate given government approval!

447
00:23:44.780 --> 00:23:47.360
I find all of the Seven
Warlords despicable,

448
00:23:47.360 --> 00:23:49.620
but Crocodile's the absolute worst.

449
00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:52.910
Politically speaking, isn't he
an ally of the World Government

450
00:23:52.910 --> 00:23:53.950
and the Marines?

451
00:23:53.950 --> 00:23:56.620
Crocodile might have
the powers that be fooled,

452
00:23:56.620 --> 00:23:57.370
but not me.

453
00:23:57.370 --> 00:24:01.000
They're delusional if they think
giving him a sanction will make him obey.

454
00:24:01.000 --> 00:24:01.710
He's a pirate!

455
00:24:02.090 --> 00:24:04.710
There's one thing you always
need to remember, Tashigi.

456
00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:07.430
A pirate's a pirate,
no matter where they go.

457
00:24:07.430 --> 00:24:09.550
They never change.

458
00:24:09.890 --> 00:24:14.060
Crocodile will lead us right to him.
Straw Hat'll show up wherever he is,

459
00:24:14.060 --> 00:24:16.890
and I'm sure we'll find out
what's going on when we get there.

460
00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:20.060
There'll be no escape
for him, not this time.

461
00:24:20.270 --> 00:24:23.070
Woo-hoo! Time to celebrate, guys!

462
00:24:20.970 --> 00:24:22.070
All right!

463
00:24:22.070 --> 00:24:25.190
Since he's one of us now,
here's to Fire Fist Ace!

464
00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:26.110
– Cheers!
– Cheers!

465
00:24:26.110 --> 00:24:28.410
Wait! Who said
I was joining your crew?!

466
00:24:30.740 --> 00:24:32.450
And to delicious drinks, eh?

467
00:24:32.450 --> 00:24:32.830
– Cheers!
– Cheers!

468
00:24:33.280 --> 00:24:34.160
Oh, don't worry.

469
00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:35.660
Here's to delicious food!

470
00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:37.160
You can't take anything they say
seriously when they're like this.

471
00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:36.910
– Cheers!
– Cheers!

472
00:24:36.910 --> 00:24:38.410
Here's to delicious medicine!

473
00:24:37.160 --> 00:24:38.580
They get all goofy when they drink.

474
00:24:38.410 --> 00:24:41.000
– Medicine isn't delicious. It's terrible!
– Medicine isn't delicious. It's terrible!

475
00:24:43.670 --> 00:24:47.630
Ace! Are you sure you don't wanna
join us? It'll be fun! I promise.

476
00:24:47.630 --> 00:24:50.090
I can't right now.
I'm chasing someone.

477
00:24:51.640 --> 00:24:53.300
He's a pirate named Blackbeard.

478
00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:54.680
Uh, Blackbeard?!

479
00:24:54.680 --> 00:24:57.270
We've heard of him. He was the one
who attacked Drum Kingdom!

480
00:24:58.100 --> 00:25:00.060
You see, Blackbeard
used to be a member

481
00:25:00.060 --> 00:25:02.360
of the Second Division
of the Whitebeard Pirates.

482
00:25:02.360 --> 00:25:03.650
He was one of my own men,

483
00:25:03.650 --> 00:25:06.280
but he committed the most
unforgivable sin a pirate could.

484
00:25:06.280 --> 00:25:08.280
He killed one of
his fellow crew members,

485
00:25:08.280 --> 00:25:09.650
and then he jumped ship.

486
00:25:09.650 --> 00:25:11.450
As commander of his division,

487
00:25:11.450 --> 00:25:14.450
it's my responsibility
to take care of him.

488
00:25:14.450 --> 00:25:16.620
So that's why you're after him.

489
00:25:17.290 --> 00:25:19.830
Exactly. We've just
entered the Sandora River.

490
00:25:19.830 --> 00:25:21.870
We'll take it to Erumalu,
where we'll dock,

491
00:25:21.870 --> 00:25:25.420
and then we'll proceed on foot
until we reach Yuba, here.

492
00:25:25.750 --> 00:25:28.800
The leader of the Rebel Army is there.
That's where we're going.

493
00:25:28.800 --> 00:25:31.380
You don't say.
Do you mind if I tag along?

494
00:25:31.840 --> 00:25:34.890
Nami, Vivi, I'll follow you anywhere!
Just tell me where to go!

495
00:25:34.890 --> 00:25:36.350
Hopefully, it's off of a cliff.

496
00:25:36.350 --> 00:25:37.720
What did you say, Zoro?!

497
00:25:37.720 --> 00:25:39.270
Cool it, you two!

498
00:25:39.270 --> 00:25:41.540
Well, looks like you'll be with us
for a little while, Ace!

499
00:25:41.540 --> 00:25:44.310
Ha, ha! We're all
really happy to have you aboard.

500
00:25:46.320 --> 00:25:47.730
This is gonna be fun!

501
00:25:47.730 --> 00:25:48.940
To Ace!

502
00:25:48.940 --> 00:25:50.820
– Cheers!
– Cheers!
